From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: premultiply theme images like XP in the external shell

Purpose: give theme images with alpha XP's exact colours.
Wine premultiplies a 32-bit theme image as colour * (alpha + 1) >> 8, which
is one more than XP's colour * alpha / 255 for some pixels: drawn onto black,
90 of 1331 pixels of Luna's radio button, check box, push button and close
button were one higher in a channel than on the reference XP machine
(tests/part-black.c), and so were the soft corners of caption buttons on
screen. AlphaBlend itself gives XP's results (tests/alpha-blend.c). With
XP's rounding in the opted-in external shell all of them are equal.

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
index 89b45bb..980daac 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -1449,7 +1449,19 @@ static BOOL prepare_alpha (HBITMAP bmp, BOOL* hasAlpha, BOOL *hasDefaultTranspar
 
     p = dib.dsBm.bmBits;
     n = dib.dsBmih.biHeight * dib.dsBmih.biWidth;
-    /* AlphaBlend() wants premultiplied alpha, so do that now */
+    /* AlphaBlend() wants premultiplied alpha, so do that now. XP truncates
+     * colour * alpha / 255; the external shell matches its pixels. */
+    if (GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0))
+    {
+        while (n-- > 0)
+        {
+            p[0] = p[0] * p[3] / 255;
+            p[1] = p[1] * p[3] / 255;
+            p[2] = p[2] * p[3] / 255;
+            p += 4;
+        }
+        return TRUE;
+    }
     while (n-- > 0)
     {
         int a = p[3]+1;
